[0.30.0] - 2026-08-25
=====================

**Changed**

  - Replaced the Node.js-based ``prettier`` markdown formatter and ``pre-commit``
    framework with ``mdformat``, a pure-Python CommonMark formatter invoked
    directly via ``uv run mdformat``.

  - Updated GitHub Actions CI (``.github/workflows/ci.yml``) and GitLab CI/CD
    (``.gitlab/ci/code_quality.yml``) workflows to verify Markdown formatting
    directly via ``uv run mdformat --check README.md``.

  - Updated ``pyproject.toml`` dev dependencies to include ``mdformat`` and
    removed ``pre-commit`` and ``.pre-commit-cache``.

**Removed**

  - Removed ``.pre-commit-config.yaml`` and ``.prettierrc``.
  - Removed ``licenses/pre_commit.md`` and ``licenses/prettier.md``.

**Docs**

  - Rewrote ``docs/developer_guide/source/developers/topics/markdown_formatting.rst``
    to document direct ``mdformat`` execution, CommonMark compliance, target
    scoping, and developer workflows.
  - Updated ``docs/developer_guide/source/developers/contributing.rst``,
    ``docs/developer_guide/source/developers/topics/project_layout.rst``,
    ``docs/developer_guide/source/developers/topics/publishing.rst``, and
    ``docs/developer_guide/source/developers/topics/index.rst`` to reflect
    ``mdformat`` usage.
  - Added ``licenses/mdformat.md`` (MIT License) and updated ``licenses/README.md``.


[0.20.0] - 2026-08-05
=====================

**Changed**

  - PyInstaller hooks: renamed ``src/extra_hooks/hook_package.py`` to
    ``src/extra_hooks/hook-scaldys_template.py`` and simplified its content.
    This change aligns with the updated hook handling in ``scaldys-project``
    v0.20.0.

    .. note::
       **Breaking change.** This version requires ``scaldys-project >= 0.20.0``
       for Windows builds due to the change in hook file naming conventions.

  - Dependencies: bumped ``scaldys-project`` to v0.20.0.


[0.12.0] - 2026-08-04
=====================

**Added**

  - GitLab CI/CD configuration: added ``.gitlab-ci.yml`` and supporting workflow
    definitions in ``.gitlab/ci/`` for quality gates, testing, and release
    automation.

  - PyInstaller hooks: added ``hook-tksvg.py`` and ``hook-ttkbootstrap.py`` to
    ``src/extra_hooks/`` for reliable asset collection in frozen builds; updated
    the generic ``hook_package.py`` to automatically collect package data files.

  - GUI assets: included FontAwesome SVG icons in the ``scaldys_template``
    package data to ensure they are available in installed environments.

**Changed**

  - GUI: enhanced the ``gui`` command with explicit exception handling and
    critical error logging during application startup.

  - GUI: improved support for frozen environments and added a mechanism to
    preserve stdout/stderr output when the ``--verbose`` flag is used.

  - CI: restricted heavy quality gates (lock file check, linting, type checking)
    to ``main`` and ``develop`` branches to optimize pipeline usage.

  - Dependencies: bumped ``typer`` to v0.27.1 and ``scaldys-project`` to v0.15.0.

  - Formatting: standardized codebase using ``ruff format``.

**Docs**

  - User guide: added troubleshooting section to the Signal Analyzer guide covering
    startup failures and the new global ``--verbose`` flag.


[0.11.0] - 2026-06-20
=====================

**Added**

  - ``__future__.annotations`` added to various modules for improved type hint
    support and forward reference handling.

  - ``WindowsSafeRotatingFileHandler``: a ``RotatingFileHandler`` subclass that
    gracefully handles Windows file-lock errors during log rollover, preventing
    crashes when a log file is held open by another process.

  - GUI: unit tests for the ``Application`` state and ``SideBar`` navigation logic.

  - GUI: unit tests for the ``ToolBar`` functionality and contextual behavior
    (``tests/unit/tk/test_toolbar.py``).

  - ``Application.update_parameters(params, source)``: central synchronisation
    method that broadcasts a ``SignalParameters`` change to both the Analyzer
    and the Editor, skipping the originating view to avoid feedback loops.

**Changed**

  - ``tksvg`` made an optional dependency; added fallback to native Tk 8.7+ SVG
    support for platforms where the binary extension is unavailable.

  - Standardized ``messagebox`` usage across GUI frames for consistent user
    interaction.

  - CI: separated Linux and non-Linux test runs; ensured tkinter-dependent
    tests are skipped in headless environments.

  - CI: improved robustness of UI example initialization and SVG handling in
    automated tests.

  - Updated ``certifi`` and ``coverage`` dependencies.

  - Refactored sash placement logic in ``AnalyzerFrame`` to ensure reliable
    layout initialization.

  - Improved FontAwesome image utilities with an explicit ``master`` parameter
    for better widget ownership control and CI environment compatibility.

  - Updated GUI test suite with support for DPI awareness and dark title bar
    logic.

  - Reconfigured the application toolbar to follow standard Windows patterns.
    Navigation-switching buttons were replaced with action buttons: "Play"
    became "Run", "Stop" became "Defaults", and the redundant "Settings" button
    was removed.  New "Open" and "Save" buttons were added.

  - Toolbar visibility management: the toolbar is fully visible in the Signal
    Analyzer, shows file operations and an "Apply" button in the JSON Editor,
    and is hidden entirely for UI Examples and Navigation frames.

  - Reconfigured the ``EditorFrame``: the "Apply" button was moved from the
    frame header to the application toolbar for better integration and visual
    consistency across frames.

  - Renamed "Play" view to "Navigation" throughout the application.

  - Renamed "Example" view to "UI Examples" throughout the application.

  - ``scaldys-project`` dependency bumped to v0.13.0.

  - SideBar: now expanded by default on startup.
  - SideBar: implemented a selection highlighting mechanism for the active frame button using the theme's primary color.
  - SideBar: selection state now automatically synchronizes with view switching in the main application.
  - SideBar: added "Editor" button (``file-lines-regular`` icon) for the new JSON
    Editor view.  Also fixed a pre-existing bug where the icon enum referenced a
    non-existent ``file-lines-solid-full.svg`` asset.

  - ``AnalyzerFrame``: the dedicated *Save parameters…* and *Load parameters…*
    buttons have been removed from the left panel.  File operations are now
    handled exclusively through the File menu.  The *Reset to defaults* button
    is retained.  An ``on_params_changed`` callback parameter has been added so
    the frame can notify ``Application`` of parameter changes without importing
    it directly.

  - ``SignalParametersFrame``: added an ``on_change`` callback parameter.  The
    callback fires on ``FocusOut`` (numeric widgets) and ``<<ComboboxSelected>>``
    (dropdowns) using a silent ``_parse_parameters()`` helper that does not
    modify the UI validation state.

  - ``MenuBar``: now accepts an ``Application`` reference; all file-related
    commands route through ``Application`` instead of ``AnalyzerFrame``.

**Docs**

  - User guide: updated Signal Analyzer documentation (Layout, Toolbar,
    Running, File management) to reflect the new toolbar functionality.

  - Developer guide: updated Signal Analyzer design notes to include
    ``ToolBar`` architecture and context management.

  - User guide: updated Signal Analyzer layout overview to include the SideBar.
  - Developer guide: updated Signal Analyzer design notes to document the new GUI testing strategy.
  - User guide: updated *Saving and loading parameters* section to document the
    new File menu, Recent Files, and JSON Editor.
  - Developer guide: updated Signal Analyzer design notes with ``EditorFrame``
    architecture, bidirectional sync pattern, and the ``Application`` file-management API.

**Fixed**

  - Resolved color loading issues for ``ttkbootstrap`` Meter on Linux CI
    environments.

  - Fixed Windows-specific menubar initialization in test fixtures.

  - Improved Windows subprocess handling by using ``sys.platform`` for more
    reliable platform detection.

  - Pyright type-checking feedback resolved across several modules.


